[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Against the grounding closure, several statements are unreachable and must be restructured away or annotated with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)': the phantom-dependent guards in cycle detection and in the topological-ordering loop can never execute, because graph membership is reconciled on removal and validation is mandated to raise NodeNotFoundError on any missing dependency before ordering or cycle analysis; the loop-top cancellation re-check duplicates the run-entry and post-wave cancellation checks and is only reachable through a thread interleaving the contract does not describe; the is_finished break taken when a wave resolves empty is dead, because the loop condition already established a non-terminal scheduler state that no between-wave operation can change; and the node-execution, retry-backoff and per-node-timeout helper bodies run exclusively on executor worker threads, which statement-coverage instrumentation does not observe, so that dispatch assumption should be annotated rather than left unmeasurable.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Under the grounding closure, unit tests are missing assertions for mandated postconditions and error branches: validation must raise NodeNotFoundError when a node references a dependency identifier that was never registered; the cycle sequence carried by CycleError must include every intermediate participant of the cycle, not only its endpoints; the longest path and cumulative weight of a graph with no nodes must be the empty sequence and zero; the transitive dependents skipped under the skip-downstream policy must include dependents reachable through more than one dependency route; after a node is removed from the graph the reported state mapping must contain only current graph members; run must raise DAGCancelledError after cancel, and when cancellation is signalled while nodes are executing the non-terminal nodes must be reported CANCELLED and the error raised; a timeout budget already exhausted at a wave boundary must raise DAGTimeoutError; and under the continue-on-error policy a run whose remaining nodes can never become runnable must still terminate with those nodes reported as skipped.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Resolve coverage audit feedback: removed the dead loop-top cancellation re-check (run-entry and post-wave checks remain) and the unreachable is_finished break in the empty-wave path; annotated the invariant-protected phantom-dependent guards in cycle detection and topological ordering with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: no phantom dependents)' since removal reconciles edges and validate() rejects missing dependencies; annotated the worker-thread-only _execute_node/_invoke_action helpers (retry backoff, per-node timeout) with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: dispatch runs exclusively on executor worker threads)'. Verified runtime behavior for success, retries, all failure policies, overall/per-node timeouts, and cancellation.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Address feedback: add tests for dangling dependency validation, full 3-node cycle sequence, empty-graph critical path, multi-route skip-downstream dependents, scheduler states after node removal, DAGCancelledError on cancel and mid-run cancellation, exhausted timeout budgets, and continue-on-error dead-end runs reporting skipped nodes.
