[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: The CHANGE note states that scheduler states after node removal were added, but the added case removes an identifier before that identifier has ever been reflected in a reported state mapping, so it passes without exercising the reconciliation requirement: the contract requires the reported state mapping to contain exactly the current graph members, and the still-unverified aspect is that an identifier whose state was already reported must stop appearing after its removal from the graph while the remaining members continue to be reported with their current states; all previously cited postconditions and error branches are otherwise now covered, so this single remaining requirement aspect is the only defect.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Address feedback: reconcile scheduler state reporting after node removal by first reporting states for all nodes, transitioning a remaining node to SUCCEEDED, removing a previously reported node, and asserting the new state mapping contains exactly the surviving graph member with its updated state.
